  "problem": "Suppose we take a random sample of size $n=96$ from a population where $72%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Find a normal approximation for the probability that more than $70%$ but less than $80%$ of the sample has the characteristic. You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.\n\n*Hint: Two tables of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.04\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.7\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9591\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9599\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9608\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.8\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9671\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9678\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9686\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.9\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9738\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9744\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9750\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.04\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3300\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3264\\,$ </